<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: IWP poised to buy British company-paper.</title>
<headline>IWP poised to buy British company-paper.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>IWP International Plc is at an advanced stage of negotiations to acquire a British manufacturer and distributor of personal care products, the Irish Times reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the company being acquired operates in the English midlands and generates annual sales of some 40 million sterling.</p>
<p>&quot;The consideration will be around 40 million but the final figure is not expected to be agreed for a couple of months,&quot; the report said.</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom 353-1-661-3377</p>
</text>
